        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Comparisons and alternatives",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "Travel guidance recommends carrying extra medication and keeping medication in carry-on luggage rather than depending on checked bags. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/management/traveling",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:e41789b9f652837547c9d6dba5215129f41a61d3e35d25c9d1b35310a4c3a9a3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:bdb686171a39667e41f14322d5a06882064ba28c767877ef2f918718faf61f4b",
            "ev:d9000b5193e9e00fdfef4fbf9fafc8749f2e3aacb7d56bc92694cbef1d686171",
            "ev:e8fae4625078fd3fcd24a6b45e422c1d422e51126f4e307ea67cb28551ce9201"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://davisphinneyfoundation.org/blog/travel-with-greater-ease-parkinsons/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In a 2014 randomized trial of 191 people with PD and daily-activity difficulties, a 10-week home occupational-therapy intervention improved self-perceived daily activity performance at 3 months compared with usual care without occupational therapy; the endpoint does not establish disease modification. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://pubmed.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/24726066/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:4f242f53682b7e1084597755107fb47c3b0f326baa485fd0a4fee235de2b2a92",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:3df8e0d999df6b23f9bebafebea3731d634a1bc70975340dbada0427b7d856ec",
            "ev:661180dfd3438bd2702234533e05af539721a063b5efcbd83c7ed17d31278b1c",
            "ev:72189d691978554938d23d1a22430d0c5098524e979eb9ddfb5813de87505262",
            "ev:a27546b494c7723322ba30bea2fdd86cfe1741b0bc461590bcc11f4f41c78b4e"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "In a Parkinson’s UK forum discussion, one traveler with PD reported that advance wheelchair assistance helped with airport queues and walking; this is an individual experience rather than evidence that one itinerary is best for everyone. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://forum.parkinsons.org.uk/t/long-distance-air-travel-uk-to-australia-advice-please/43760",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:d45aff1cf16b1ffd32680b85bc6f1ae3b0c904ea54b0b06bd32b2bd7a1e42d3e",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:447ae74f8d4430b3c3a0a80757d67ede94620c99de082ed3f11a586769a3a346"
          ]
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "title": "Facts and statements",
      "facts": [
        {
          "text": "A PD diagnosis alone does not determine whether someone can drive safely; the Parkinson’s Foundation advises assessment of the individual’s symptoms and other age-related changes. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/management/activities-daily-living/driving",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:f8ee3ae05661a5e8859a08f11262da4fb044c1b32de5f820375af370b9801dba",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5dac6ef1c335e94164f942a7713f03bec11b1682585284bd27d3a2775b674b3a"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Driving fitness assessment should consider motor function, cognition, vision, sleepiness and medication effects; specialist on-road and off-road assessment can help resolve concerns. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://pmc.ncbi.nlm.nih.gov/articles/PMC10928339/",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:68a1c630a8ce960dc91bc6c6be473fe70eeb90e691cc4b407d75950d167a47b4",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:aec00bf0bf3a3f751b669e70a37a7514fca94e704d4204e75f933e6d518a8a50",
            "ev:fce86b4dbaab6ddb197be9ccb0837dd47a2486181bd835e8b931da8e6365241a"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/management/activities-daily-living/driving"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "For time-zone travel, the Parkinson’s Foundation advises preserving the prescribed intervals between doses; Davis Phinney Foundation travel guidance likewise recommends planning a consistent medication schedule. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/management/traveling",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:80f284ed1a2fdfbf178e008a3c75c3894cb6171a1403f416324a113f853ffc4d",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:aa0c96d8032d44962496e98cdcf1d64a29bdf9afebe2d44b27af1edd54506023",
            "ev:b2512ccd96ac66899ff562095d6acf7354d9db97a3b6ef875ef5355db8edee09"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://davisphinneyfoundation.org/blog/travel-with-greater-ease-parkinsons/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Travel planning guidance recommends allowing extra time, scheduling rest around arrival, and avoiding an overloaded itinerary. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/management/traveling",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:768bdebc94b87fb4b5126c9cb9a6a6178bf781d95ca60eaa08da734631e955af",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:50e68156b9228bd733a5e5c558efc80e9e46256279901a515d15c355b637a94e",
            "ev:5875d77194344d82ea240ce91f4a2415ddf381e7360265840288ee40d435a0c9",
            "ev:f91f512225b39f6a551534d089e3eba3e37c5e935d3533bafc410b3f9cb6f5fb"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://davisphinneyfoundation.org/blog/travel-with-greater-ease-parkinsons/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "How long a person continues working after PD diagnosis varies with job demands, symptoms and circumstances; Parkinson’s Europe describes contrasting personal experiences of continuing work and leaving work. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/library/fact-sheets/employment",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:18ab9063ba5a94b5f184816534d9bab8316cc20b28c7024551c26a737f0c5df3",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:87bac94d6f892c428323b4ce04c759696aecbe972d04953733992f4e57643d5f",
            "ev:ae7c864bea3a679b529eee0b7fecee30638aaddb92e21c766853de32e8e9e93d",
            "ev:f59e0fa3249370919554123c3400e09ac0ea3727ecbe073201bf96da6c4e1683"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://parkinsonseurope.org/parkinsonslife/navigating-the-workplace-with-parkinsons-disease/"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Suggested workplace adaptations include scheduling difficult tasks during better-functioning periods, breaks, ergonomic or computer adaptations, and exploring flexible hours or telecommuting where feasible. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/library/fact-sheets/employment",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:fb550064a42e0367fb7581b72586731e5c73b396bfc61239ddf3ea74dda434ce",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:5bfee26a2e49712b16acfaefc9cbd0a6658002d07f50f21d246ccc03c8732cd7",
            "ev:c67c7b4fc3a0f7d932f1331e55ac1437b40dff46f986f433a43ebc832563a128"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "Occupational therapy can tailor routines and task strategies to a person’s priorities, including dressing, cooking, handwriting, work and driving; the plan is tested and adjusted to the person’s needs. (medium confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.parkinson.org/library/fact-sheets/occupational-therapy",
          "note": null,
          "claimId": "clm:3d6c18a1711f5a51c4be516a4173cf1131e998b597c7e37f2e14a49d22cecd4b",
          "validationStatus": "SUPPORTED",
          "evidenceIds": [
            "ev:31dc2e0ee318254ca7443e62032c279173dca4b0d44fcaad73e7325af415e040",
            "ev:4d42956ccc9532041c7d025e7ae685b23d3319c5eeca6b671abde8c95b67c52e",
            "ev:8d47da6f30c9b7e51d75e8703439b5d3b7145f19c0923821e2786858179c4e5f",
            "ev:c82ce84f579bdb326d40512d7b4850db960b971631bcc0283257c5cc28392098",
            "ev:c846988d99d833fb34b4cad3144276c4e23c880b728b9675641277a0da314675",
            "ev:e34d7aae69fbc89da0af8285f945181a1401ee7f87b6f5f0c5455026657f5ab1"
          ],
          "also": [
            "https://www.parkinson.org/living-with-parkinsons/treatment/physical-occupational-speech-therapies"
          ]
        },
        {
          "text": "A 2018 driving meta-analysis found poorer on-road and simulator outcomes in PD, but no significant difference in self-reported real-life crash involvement; its authors cautioned against PD-specific relicensure mandates based on self-reported crash data alone. (low confidence)",
          "source": "https://www.neurology.org/doi/10.1212/WNL.0000000000006132",
          "note": null,
